<title>USA: U.S. FAA veteran named acting deputy administrator.</title>
<headline>U.S. FAA veteran named acting deputy administrator.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>A career Federal Aviation Administration official, Monte Belger, has been named acting deputy administrator, succeeding Linda Hall Daschle, who is now the agency's acting administrator.</p>
<p>Belger, a 24-year FAA veteran, is the agency's associate administrator for air traffic services, heading a staff of 35,000 who operate the nation's air-traffic control system.</p>
<p>Daschle was given an interim appointment as administrator when David Hinson resigned on November 8. She is to remain in her post until January 31, when she will leave the agency.</p>
</text>
